' =====================================================================
'  10. NOTES & LEGEND
' =====================================================================
note as N1
  **OOP principles in this design**
  1. *Encapsulation* - private fields (-) + private helper methods;
     entities hide passwordHash from SELECTs.
  2. *Abstraction* - ImageStorage abstract class, DTO/mapper interfaces.
  3. *Inheritance* - HttpException -> domain errors;
     ImageStorage -> Local/Cloudinary strategies.
  4. *Polymorphism* - guards implement CanActivate, interceptor
     implements NestInterceptor, filter implements ExceptionFilter;
     NestJS invokes them uniformly.
  5. *Dependency Inversion / DI* - every collaborator is constructor
     injected; services depend on abstractions, not concretes.
  6. *Separation of concerns* - Controller (HTTP) -> Service (logic)
     -> Repository/Entity (persistence); DTOs in, DTOs out.
end note

note bottom of User
  Entities are **anemic** (verified in source): no methods,
  only columns + navigation properties. All behaviour is in
  the service layer.
end note

legend bottom
  |= Notation |= Meaning |
  | + / - / # / ~ | public / private / protected / package |
  | italic name | interface or abstract class |
  | «stereotype» | NestJS role: @Injectable, @Controller, @Catch, DTO, entity |
  | {abstract} {static} | member modifiers |
  | ..|> | implements (interface) |
  | --|> | extends (class inheritance) |
  | *-- | composition (cascade delete) |
  | -->> | directed association (foreign key) |
  | ..> | dependency / uses |
  | "1" "0..*" | multiplicity |
end legend

